WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.582
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A two.

2
00:00:05.882 --> 00:00:09.199
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.499 --> 00:00:17.004
Unit twenty-six: Present Perfect vs Past Simple. Today you will choose the right tense for finished and unfinished time.

4
00:00:17.304 --> 00:00:20.061
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.477
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.317 --> 00:00:26.318
Finished time.

7
00:00:27.317 --> 00:00:30.617
Finished time means a time that is completely in the past.

8
00:00:31.217 --> 00:00:33.065
Last year is a finished time.

9
00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:36.430
Your turn. Say: Finished time.

10
00:00:39.267 --> 00:00:40.454
Finished time.

11
00:00:41.217 --> 00:00:42.485
Unfinished time.

12
00:00:43.483 --> 00:00:46.388
Unfinished time means a time that includes the present.

13
00:00:46.983 --> 00:00:48.948
Today is an unfinished time.

14
00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:52.144
Your turn. Say: Unfinished time.

15
00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:56.640
Unfinished time.

16
00:00:57.383 --> 00:00:58.524
Yesterday.

17
00:00:59.517 --> 00:01:01.656
Yesterday means the day before today.

18
00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:03.774
I went there yesterday.

19
00:01:04.383 --> 00:01:06.734
Your turn. Say: Yesterday.

20
00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:10.566
Yesterday.

21
00:01:11.317 --> 00:01:12.376
Last year.

22
00:01:13.383 --> 00:01:15.720
Last year means the year before this one.

23
00:01:16.317 --> 00:01:17.712
We moved last year.

24
00:01:18.317 --> 00:01:21.132
Your turn. Say: Last year.

25
00:01:23.967 --> 00:01:25.003
Last year.

26
00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:26.530
Just.

27
00:01:27.517 --> 00:01:29.563
Just means a very short time ago.

28
00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:31.499
I have just arrived.

29
00:01:32.083 --> 00:01:34.353
Your turn. Say: Just.

30
00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:38.131
Just.

31
00:01:38.883 --> 00:01:39.861
Recently.

32
00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:42.710
Recently means not long ago.

33
00:01:43.317 --> 00:01:45.456
I have recently started a course.

34
00:01:46.050 --> 00:01:48.842
Your turn. Say: Recently.

35
00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:52.817
Recently.

36
00:01:53.583 --> 00:01:54.793
Result now.

37
00:01:55.783 --> 00:01:59.524
Result now means a present situation caused by a past action.

38
00:02:00.117 --> 00:02:02.615
I have lost my keys, so I can't enter.

39
00:02:03.217 --> 00:02:05.765
Your turn. Say: Result now.

40
00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:09.915
Result now.

41
00:02:10.650 --> 00:02:11.860
Experience.

42
00:02:12.850 --> 00:02:15.720
Experience means something that you have done in your life.

43
00:02:16.317 --> 00:02:18.096
Travel is an experience.

44
00:02:18.683 --> 00:02:21.754
Your turn. Say: Experience.

45
00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:25.868
Experience.

46
00:02:26.667 --> 00:02:30.271
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:31.117 --> 00:02:34.974
Visal, did you visit Siem Reap last year, or have you visited Siem Reap?

48
00:02:36.083 --> 00:02:47.295
Both are possible. Did you visit last year uses the past simple because last year is a finished time. Have you visited uses the present perfect because the time is not named.

49
00:02:48.383 --> 00:02:49.721
How do we choose?

50
00:02:50.817 --> 00:03:09.351
Past simple: finished time words like yesterday, last year, in 2020, two days ago. Present perfect: no time, or an unfinished time like today, this week, ever, never, just and recently.

51
00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:12.287
Can you give a pair of examples?

52
00:03:13.383 --> 00:03:26.304
I visited Siem Reap in 2022 (finished). I have visited Siem Reap twice (experience). I lost my keys yesterday. I have lost my keys (and I still can't find them: result now).

53
00:03:27.467 --> 00:03:29.362
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:30.217 --> 00:03:33.969
Grammar focus: Present perfect vs past simple.

55
00:03:34.269 --> 00:03:35.445
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:38.080
I visited Siem Reap last year.

57
00:03:38.983 --> 00:03:41.215
I have visited Siem Reap twice.

58
00:03:42.117 --> 00:03:43.838
She has just finished her homework.

59
00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:52.770
Use the past simple with finished time words and the present perfect with no time or unfinished time. Just and recently go with the present perfect.

60
00:03:53.517 --> 00:03:56.668
Be careful! Don't say: I have seen him yesterday.

61
00:03:58.633 --> 00:04:00.586
Say: I saw him yesterday.

62
00:04:00.886 --> 00:04:02.840
Use past simple with yesterday.

63
00:04:03.633 --> 00:04:06.193
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:08.129
Which Tense?.

65
00:04:08.429 --> 00:04:12.054
I visited Siem Reap last year, and I have visited it twice.

66
00:04:13.067 --> 00:04:17.005
My sister lost her keys yesterday, and she has not found them yet.

67
00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:20.940
I have just finished my homework, so I can relax.

68
00:04:21.933 --> 00:04:24.780
We moved to this town in 2021.

69
00:04:25.767 --> 00:04:29.322
Finished time words, such as yesterday, need the past simple.

70
00:04:30.433 --> 00:04:34.656
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:35.517 --> 00:04:36.947
I blank him yesterday.

72
00:04:37.247 --> 00:04:40.564
A, have seen. B, saw. C, have saw.

73
00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:45.914
The answer is B: saw.

74
00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:48.574
She blank just arrived.

75
00:04:48.874 --> 00:04:51.865
A, has. B, have. C, did.

76
00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:57.156
The answer is A: has.

77
00:04:58.317 --> 00:05:00.502
Which time word needs the past simple?

78
00:05:00.802 --> 00:05:04.258
A, ever. B, last year. C, recently.

79
00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:09.672
The answer is B: last year.

80
00:05:10.817 --> 00:05:12.538
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:05:12.838 --> 00:05:20.334
A, I have been there in 2020.. B, I went there in 2020.. C, I have gone there in 2020..

82
00:05:23.900 --> 00:05:27.037
The answer is B: I went there in 2020..

83
00:05:28.183 --> 00:05:31.634
According to the reading, when did the family move to the town?

84
00:05:31.934 --> 00:05:36.540
A, in 2021. B, yesterday. C, just now.

85
00:05:40.100 --> 00:05:43.121
The answer is A: in 2021.

86
00:05:44.333 --> 00:05:47.659
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:48.517 --> 00:05:52.211
Write one sentence in the past simple and one in the present perfect.

88
00:06:01.017 --> 00:06:02.761
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:03.061 --> 00:06:17.050
I visited Phnom Penh last year. I have visited it three times. The first sentence is in the past simple because last year is finished. The second is in the present perfect because I talk about my experience.

90
00:06:17.350 --> 00:06:19.198
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:20.083 --> 00:06:25.011
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and present perfect vs past simple.

92
00:06:25.311 --> 00:06:29.125
Today's value is precision. Choose your words and numbers with care.

93
00:06:29.425 --> 00:06:32.309
See you in Unit twenty-seven. Goodbye!

94
00:06:32.609 --> 00:06:35.424
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

